# CODEOWNERS — review routing for the debugging-generator monorepo
#
# GitHub reads this file to request reviews from the owners of the paths a pull
# request changes. It is also the repository's area map: each block below names
# one area of the monorepo and says why a change there deserves its reviewer.
# What each area is and how the areas fit together is described in
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md (sections 2 and 3).
#
# OWNERS ARE PLACEHOLDERS. The repository declares no GitHub user or team, so
# every rule names the single placeholder owner @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER, which is
# not a real account. Until it is replaced:
#   - this file is inert: no review is requested from anyone;
#   - GitHub reports the placeholder as an unknown owner when it validates this
#     file (the error list shown when viewing CODEOWNERS on GitHub).
# To activate it:
#   - replace the placeholder with a GitHub user handle or an organisation team
#     (organisation/team form), and that user or team must have write access to
#     the repository, or GitHub ignores the rule;
#   - replace PER AREA, not with one global search-and-replace, so each block
#     routes to the people who own that area;
#   - enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection rule or
#     ruleset for the protected branches; without it reviews are requested but
#     not enforced.
# Never use an email address as an owner: every tracked file, this one
# included, is scanned by `pnpm check:secrets`, and review routing needs only
# handles.
#
# SYNTAX RULES THAT DECIDE THE ORDER OF THIS FILE
#   - The LAST matching pattern wins. Rules therefore run from the broadest to
#     the most specific; a specific rule placed above a broader one is dead.
#   - Patterns follow gitignore syntax, except that negation and bracketed
#     character ranges are not supported, so neither is used here.
#   - A leading slash anchors a pattern to the repository root, so no rule can
#     match a same-named folder nested inside a workspace. A trailing slash
#     names a whole directory; a path without one names a single file.
#   - GitHub uses only the first CODEOWNERS file it finds (.github/, the root,
#     docs/). This is the only one; do not add a second copy elsewhere.
#
# Nothing in this file names the demo application's components, services,
# hooks or route paths: the demo's internals are documented only in
# docs/DEMO.md.

# Catch-all: every path not matched by a more specific rule below, including
# the workspace editor settings under .vscode/.
*                                           @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Root tooling and the dependency manifest. Review the lockfile together with
# any manifest change: both land in the same commit, and the lockfile is only
# ever regenerated by `pnpm install`, never hand-edited. The runtime pins
# (.nvmrc, .node-version, packageManager) must move together.
/package.json                               @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/pnpm-lock.yaml                             @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/pnpm-workspace.yaml                        @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/.npmrc                                     @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/.nvmrc                                     @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/.node-version                              @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# TypeScript solution and base config: strict settings apply to every workspace.
/tsconfig.base.json                         @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/tsconfig.json                              @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# eslint.config.js mechanically enforces the package dependency layering (one
# no-restricted-imports block per workspace), so a change here is an
# architecture change, not a style change.
/eslint.config.js                           @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# Test runners: Vitest projects and the Playwright browser and e2e projects.
/vitest.config.ts                           @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/playwright.config.ts                       @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# Formatting and whitespace conventions.
/.prettierrc.json                           @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/.prettierignore                            @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/.editorconfig                              @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# Ignore rules and the example environment: .gitignore keeps dependencies,
# build output, session databases and every real .env file out of git.
/.gitignore                                 @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/.env.example                               @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# Local PostgreSQL for the demo only; containers are not part of the product.
/docker-compose.yml                         @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Shared packages, general.
/packages/                                  @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Cross-process schema packages. They define the contracts shared by all four
# processes (VS Code extension host, local service, Chrome MV3 extension,
# target dev server). A type that crosses a process boundary is defined here
# exactly once, and a second definition of one of these shapes in an app is a
# defect, so changes here need contract-level review. protocol sits above the
# other three and nothing below it may import it.
/packages/protocol/                         @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/telemetry/                        @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/instrumentation/                  @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/panel-schema/                     @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Single-definition schema sources: the exact files and directories where each
# cross-process shape is defined.
/packages/shared/src/source-location.ts     @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/telemetry/src/schema/             @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/instrumentation/src/schema/       @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/panel-schema/src/                 @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/protocol/src/messages/            @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/protocol/src/envelope.ts          @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/protocol/src/http.ts              @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/protocol/src/session-record.ts    @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/packages/protocol/src/analysis.ts          @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Surfaces: the three product apps. Both extensions import only the protocol
# package, never local-service internals. The demo application has its own
# block below.
/apps/                                      @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/apps/vscode-extension/                     @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/apps/chrome-extension/                     @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/apps/local-service/                        @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Versioned model prompts. A committed prompt file is immutable: a change is a
# new vNNN+1.md plus an update to prompts/manifest.json, so reject any edit to
# an existing vNNN.md in review. No prompt strings live in modules.
/apps/local-service/prompts/                @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Demo application: an instrumentation target only. It must declare no
# dependency on any product package of the debuggen workspace scope and contain
# no product hooks, and the product must contain no knowledge of it. Where its
# seeded defects live is documented only in docs/DEMO.md; never repeat that
# here or anywhere else.
/apps/demo-app/                             @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Guard scripts behind `pnpm check:no-hardcoding`, `pnpm check:secrets` and
# `pnpm check:no-residual-instrumentation`, plus the dev-server and agent-copy
# helpers and their tests.
/scripts/                                   @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# No-hardcoding policy. Machine-generated from the demo application's code
# index and committed so it is reviewed in the pull request; the check fails
# the build when the committed policy is stale. Regenerate it only with
# `pnpm check:no-hardcoding --update`; never hand-edit it.
/scripts/no-hardcoding.policy.json          @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# The only human-curated input to that policy. Allowlisting a demo-specific
# identifier here would let the product encode demo knowledge and defeat the
# generalization acceptance test, so every addition needs deliberate review.
/scripts/no-hardcoding.allowlist.json       @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# The only exemption channel for the secrets scanner. Adding a literal here is
# a security decision; a real credential must never be added.
/scripts/check-secrets.allowlist.json       @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Tests: browser and end-to-end suites, fixtures and the tests tsconfig.
/tests/                                     @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# Generalization target and independent corpus for the no-hardcoding policy:
# it must share no symbol names with the demo application.
/tests/fixtures/sample-next-app/            @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# CI and repository governance. Every action is pinned by commit SHA, and no
# step may archive, cache or upload .git/ (the checkout's remote configuration
# must never leave the runner).
/.github/                                   @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER

# Documentation, last so it wins over every broader match above.
/docs/                                      @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/README.md                                  @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
# SECURITY.md at the root is a pointer; docs/SECURITY.md is the authoritative
# security and privacy model.
/SECURITY.md                                @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/docs/SECURITY.md                           @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/LICENSE                                    @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
/apps/vscode-extension/CHANGELOG.md         @OWNER_PLACEHOLDER
